<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">bonds</ansi>

Companions come to feel something for one another. Each pair has a bond,
a number from -100 to 100, that you can read in words: "trusts Ysolde",
"can't stand Merek". It rises when they camp together, win beside each
other, agree about your choices and step in for each other. It falls when
their temperaments clash or they disagree.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Reading them</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bonds</ansi>               every pair, strongest feeling first, with what it does
  <ansi fg="command">bonds [member]</ansi>       the pairs that one companion is in
  <ansi fg="command">company inspect [member]</ansi>  one line of the same

In the web client the Company window has a Bonds tab with a bar for each
pair. It fits a phone as it does the desktop. Reading it costs nothing,
even in a fight. Only companions who are people have bonds; creatures,
constructs and the fallen have none, and the leader has loyalty instead
(<ansi fg="command">help alignment</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The words</ansi>

   75 and up      like kin: steps in twice a battle for the other
   50 to 74       close: steps in once a battle
   25 to 49       trusts: steps in once a battle
  -24 to 24       still getting to know each other
  -49 to -25      wary of: no effect in battle
  -84 to -50      can't stand: will not guard the other
  -85 and down    cannot bear: will not guard, and a warning is given

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What raises and lowers a bond</ansi>

  A camp rest together     +2 for temperaments that suit (stoic and devout,
                           cheerful and boastful, wry and grim...), +1
                           for the rest, -1 for ones that clash (cheerful
                           and grim, devout and wry, stoic and boastful),
                           and one less again when their alignments are far
                           apart. Once every half hour at most.
  A battle won together    +1 for each pair left standing, unless their
                           temperaments clash. Once every ten minutes.
  Banter                   a pair of friends or rivals sometimes talk about
                           each other (<ansi fg="command">help banter</ansi>): +1 or -1, once every
                           half hour.
  Your choices             two companions who both liked or both disliked
                           something you did (<ansi fg="command">help opinions</ansi>) gain 1; one who
                           liked it and one who did not lose 1.
  Stepping in              +3 when one guards the other in a battle. Once an
                           hour for a pair.
  A refused guard          -2 when a guardian you set to guard a rival
                           lets the blow fall. Once an hour for a pair.

Time together alone raises a bond to 50 at most, and lowers one to -50 at
most. Past 50 takes stepping in for each other, and past -50 takes real
clashes: a refused guard, or a pair already at odds disagreeing about
something you did. A company that merely travels together settles into
trust or wariness, never into a feud.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">In a battle</ansi>

  - A friend (a bond of 25 or more) in reach of a friend who is at 40%
    health or less steps in for them, whatever its role: once a battle, or
    twice for kin, and no more than two such steps a battle for the whole
    company. The log says "steps in front of Tamsin for a friend (bond
    guard)", and the web client's battle feed says the same.
  - A guardian set to guard a rival (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>) will not: "lets the blow fall
    on Garrick (no guard: they can't stand each other)", said once a
    battle. A guardian with no ward set passes over a rival when it picks
    the most hurt ally.
  - Nothing else changes. No one is stronger for a bond, and no one is
    weaker for a rivalry except by the guard that is not given.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">A rivalry at its end</ansi>

When a bond falls to -85 you are told that the two can hardly stand to
share a company. If it keeps falling to -100, one of them leaves: the one
with less loyalty (the newer one, if they are even), as if their loyalty
had run out (<ansi fg="command">help alignment</ansi>). A pair that recovers to -60 or better is
forgiven the warning. To mend one, set a guardian's ward to someone else
(a rival's refusal costs the bond each hour), and let them camp, win and
agree about your choices.

Bonds are saved with the company and kept through logging out. A companion
who leaves or is dismissed takes their bonds with them. Bonds give no gold,
experience or power, and they never move the world's clock.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help opinions</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help banter</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>.
